IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`

-- First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000 (SA) -- ss 3-6, the terms the Act defines and the Stamp Duties
-- Act shares, and the parties and acts of the grant's regulative rules. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE.
--
-- WHY THE TWO ACTS SHARE THIS MODULE. Stamp Duties Act s 71DD(12): "a person will be taken to have held a relevant
-- interest in land ... if the person is taken to have held a relevant interest in the land for the purposes of the
-- First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000"; s 71DD(13): "home has the same meaning as in the First Home and
-- Housing Construction Grants Act 2000; new home has the same meaning as in" that Act. So sda-home.l4 and
-- fhog-grant.l4 both IMPORT this module, and the s 71DD relief and the grant read "home", "new home" and "relevant
-- interest" from one place. "Spouse" and "domestic partner" are NOT shared: the Stamp Duties Act uses its own s 2
-- definitions (NOTES.md, finding 9).
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- through the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0). The deposited text is AS AT 2025-02-13 (scraped 2025-03-10),
-- at ../../../first-home-and-housing-construction-grants-act-2000/registers/source-bundle/; the Current Titles list
-- of 22 September 2026 lists a version of 4.12.2025, so a later version exists. Not the official text; may be out of
-- date.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 (new home, substantially renovated home, residential property, permanent resident,
-- Australian citizen, close personal relationship), s 4 (home), s 5(1)-(3) (owner, relevant interest), s 6 (spouse,
-- domestic partner, the separated spouse).
-- NOT ENCODED: s 5(4)-(6) (non-conforming interests, housing construction grants), s 6A (HomeBuilder grants).
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000 -- the shared terms (ss 3-6)`

§§ `s 4 -- home`

-- s 4: "A home is a building (affixed to land) that -- (a) may lawfully be used as a place of residence; and (b) is, in
-- the Commissioner's opinion, a suitable building for use as a place of residence." (b) is the Commissioner's opinion,
-- answered conditionally.
GIVEN `the building is affixed to land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may lawfully be used as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is suitable for use as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building is a home (s 4)` IF
        `the building is affixed to land`
    AND `it may lawfully be used as a place of residence`
    AND `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is suitable for use as a place of residence`

§§ `s 3 -- new home and substantially renovated home`

-- s 3: "new home means a home that has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence and includes a
-- substantially renovated home"; "substantially renovated home -- a home is a substantially renovated home if -- (a) the
-- sale of the home is, under the A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 of the Commonwealth, a taxable supply
-- as a sale of new residential premises within the meaning of section 40-75(1)(b) ...; and (b) the home, as renovated,
-- has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence". The GST Act test is a borrowed term: a FACT.
GIVEN `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home is a new home (s 3)` IF
        (NOT `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`)
    OR  (    `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)`
         AND (NOT `the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence`))

§§ `s 3 -- residential property`

-- s 3: "residential property -- land in Australia is residential property at a particular time if there is, at that
-- time, a building on the land lawfully occupied as a place of residence or suitable for occupation as a place of
-- residence".
GIVEN `the land is in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a building on it lawfully occupied as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a building on it suitable for occupation as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is residential property (s 3)` IF
        `the land is in Australia`
    AND (   `there is a building on it lawfully occupied as a place of residence`
         OR `there is a building on it suitable for occupation as a place of residence`)

§§ `s 5 -- owner and relevant interest`

-- s 5(2): "Each of the following is, subject to subsection (3), a relevant interest in land: (a) an estate in fee simple
-- in the land; or (b) a life estate in the land approved by the Commissioner; or (c) a perpetual lease of the land
-- granted by the Commonwealth or the State; or (d) a leasehold interest ... granted by the Commonwealth or the State that
-- may be converted ... into an estate in fee simple; or (e) an interest as purchaser under a contract for the purchase
-- from the Commonwealth or the State of an estate in fee simple in the land by instalments; or (f) a licence or right of
-- occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the State that gives, in the Commissioner's opinion, ... reasonable security
-- of tenure; or (g) an interest in a company's shares if the Commissioner is satisfied that -- (i) the interest entitles
-- the holder ... to exclusive occupation of a specified home owned by the company; and (ii) the value of the shares is not
-- less than the value of the company's interest in the home."
DECLARE `Kind of interest in land` IS ONE OF
    `an estate in fee simple`
    `a life estate approved by the Commissioner`
    `a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the State`
    `a Crown leasehold convertible into fee simple`
    `an interest as purchaser by instalments from the Commonwealth or the State`
    `a Crown licence or right of occupancy giving, in the Commissioner's opinion, reasonable security of tenure`
    `company shares the Commissioner is satisfied give exclusive occupation of a home and are worth at least the company's interest in it`
    `some other interest`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of interest in land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is listed in s 5(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `some other interest` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 5(3): "(a) an interest is not a relevant interest at a particular time unless the holder of the interest has, or
-- will have within 12 months after that time (or a longer time allowed by the Commissioner), a right to immediate
-- occupation of the land; (b) an interest is not a relevant interest in the hands of a person who holds it subject to a
-- trust; (c) an equitable interest is not a relevant interest unless it is the interest of a person under a legal
-- disability for whom a guardian holds the interest on trust." The s 5(4) non-conforming interests (Regulations 2015,
-- reg 4) are not encoded.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of interest in land`
      `the holder has or will have within 12 months (or longer allowed) a right to immediate occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder holds it subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is held on trust by a guardian for a person under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` IF
        `the kind is listed in s 5(2)` `the kind`
    AND `the holder has or will have within 12 months (or longer allowed) a right to immediate occupation`
    AND (NOT `the holder holds it subject to a trust`)
    AND (    (NOT `it is an equitable interest`)
         OR  `it is held on trust by a guardian for a person under a legal disability`)

-- s 5(1): "A person is an owner of a home or a home owner if the person has a relevant interest in land on which a home
-- is built."
GIVEN `the person has a relevant interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a home is built on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an owner of a home (s 5(1))` IF
        `the person has a relevant interest in the land`
    AND `a home is built on the land`

§§ `s 6 -- spouse and domestic partner`

-- s 6(1): "A person is the spouse of another if they are legally married." (1a): "A person is the domestic partner of
-- another if they live together in a close personal relationship." s 3: "close personal relationship means the
-- relationship between 2 adult persons ... who live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis, but does not
-- include -- (a) the relationship between a legally married couple; or (b) a relationship where 1 of the persons provides
-- the other with domestic support or personal care ... for fee or reward". s 6(2): if the Commissioner is satisfied the
-- applicant "(a) is legally married but not cohabiting with the person to whom the applicant is legally married; and
-- (b) has no intention of resuming cohabitation, the person ... is not to be regarded as the applicant's spouse."
GIVEN `they are legally married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they cohabit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant intends to resume cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is the applicant's spouse (s 6(1), (2))` IF
        `they are legally married`
    AND (`they cohabit` OR `the applicant intends to resume cohabitation`)

GIVEN `they are legally married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are two adults living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one provides the other with domestic support or personal care for fee or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is the applicant's domestic partner (s 6(1a))` IF
        (NOT `they are legally married`)
    AND `they are two adults living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis`
    AND (NOT `one provides the other with domestic support or personal care for fee or reward`)

§§ `Regulative rules of the grant -- the parties and the acts`

-- The Commissioner of State Taxation, the Treasurer and the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal are
-- parties to rules, never seats.
DECLARE `Grant party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `a complying applicant, the others exempted by the Commissioner`
    `the Commissioner of State Taxation`
    `the Treasurer`

DECLARE `Grant act` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Commissioner for the grant`
    `give the applicant notice of the decision on the application`
    `begin to live in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence`
    `stop living in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence`
    `give the Commissioner written notice that the residence requirement was not complied with`
    `repay the amount of the grant`
    `repay the amount required by the notice`
    `lodge a written notice of objection with the Treasurer`
    `give the objector written notice of the decision on the objection`
    `seek a review by the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal`
